       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. Acetaminophen 5000 mg three times daily comes to 15 g per day, which is almost four times the usual maximum of 4 g per day. For a 70 kg adult, a single 5 g dose is already above the recommended single dose (about 1 g). A regimen like this carries a serious risk of fatal hepatotoxicity, even with normal liver function.\n\nThis may be a typo. Did you mean one of these?\n- **500 mg PO TID** (1.5 g/day)\n- **650 mg PO TID** (1.95 g/day)\n- **1000 mg PO TID** (3 g/day)\n\nIf you meant a different dose or frequency, tell me the dose, route and frequency and I'll enter it. If you really do want 5000 mg TID, please confirm that and give me the clinical rationale. I would still be reluctant to enter it as written without a pharmacist review."
      }
