     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I won't enter this order as written, even with your confirmation. Acetaminophen 5000 mg three times daily is 15 g per day. That is a potentially lethal dose, and I can't think of a clinical situation where it would be appropriate. It risks acute liver failure, and kidney and liver function being normal doesn't change that.\n\nI haven't placed anything in the system. These are some options:\n- **Enter a safe dose now.** For example, 1000 mg PO three times daily (3 g/day) or 650 mg PO every 6 hours. Tell me which one and I'll enter it right away.\n- **Review it with pharmacy.** If you think there's an unusual indication, a pharmacist or toxicology consult is the right way to review it. They can enter it through their own process if they agree.\n- **Check for a unit or entry error.** Mix-ups between mg and other units, or an extra zero, are a common cause of overdose orders.\n\nLet me know which option you'd like."
      }
     ],
